Rules in force for shadowed
File: $T/proj/agent.yaml
Tier: landlock

Can read: Files the agent can open and read.
  Can read any other file on this computer, except the ones under Never reads and Always on.

Can change: Files and folders the agent can create, edit or delete.
  - Can change files in ./work/  [Enforced by the operating system; line 6; editable]
  Cannot change anything else.

Never reads: Files the agent can never open, whatever it tries.
  - Can never read files in ./work/secrets/  [Not enforced for this run: it lies inside a folder the agent can change; line 8; editable]

Programs: The programs the agent can start.
  - Can run bash  [Enforced by the operating system; line 12; editable]
  Cannot run any other program.

Network: Where the agent can connect.
  Cannot connect anywhere.

Settings it gets: Environment variables the agent starts with, by name. Values are never shown here.
  Gets every variable in your shell, secrets included.

Limits: When the run is stopped or slowed down.
  No limits of its own: this computer's defaults apply.

Always on: Protections every run gets, written in no rules file.
  - Can never read the usual secret files: SSH and cloud keys, browser profiles, .env files and similar  [Enforced by the operating system; built in]
  - Can never change files that would run code outside the agent: git hooks, shell startup files and agent settings  [Best effort: tego refuses it, but a program built to race tego could get past; built in]
  - Can never read or change tego's records of its runs  [Enforced by the operating system; built in]
  - Cannot change its own rules file  [Enforced by the operating system; built in]
  - Can read this computer's network setup: interface names and addresses, routes, and the nearby machines it has talked to  [built in]
  - Cannot gain root through sudo or other setuid programs  [Enforced by the operating system; built in]
  - Writes every refusal and question to a record that cannot be changed unnoticed, and a summary of the rest  [built in]

Rule keys:
  change fs.write fs.write[./work/] enforced
  never-read fs.deny_read fs.deny_read[./work/secrets/] not_enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[bash] enforced
  always-on built-in.deny_read fs.deny_read[$T/home/.ssh] enforced (+1 more)
  always-on built-in.deny_write fs.deny_write[$T/proj/work/.git/hooks] best_effort
  always-on built-in.route-read route-query none
